{"task":"Merge master: adopt its bare-wins precedence, keep the single mode","goals":"Reconcile the mode consolidation with master's suffix-dropping and README rewrite","status":"Waiting","recorded_at":"2026-09-09T20:21:29Z","body":"Master (7efdd20) dropped the .ldev folder suffix and rewrote the README while this branch\nwas collapsing the serving modes. Both touched the same four files, and the two changes\ndisagreed about one thing that matters: which folder wins when shop/ and shop.ldev/ both\nexist. Master says the plain one, settled with Bryce directly. This branch said the\nsuffixed one. Master wins, and it is the better answer — the suffix was never\nload-bearing, so the folder that needs no renaming should be the one that serves.\n\nTaken from master, not reimplemented:\n\n  - the wildcard block's precedence, which is neater than what was here. An unconditional\n    `root * <sites>/{labels.1}.<tld>` followed by `@plain file` and `root @plain` lets the\n    last matching root win, in place of the four matcher/handle pairs this branch grew.\n  - site_host(), which takes a path rather than a basename and quotes the TLD in its glob\n  - the shadowed-folder warnings in `ldev list` and `ldev doctor`, and `ldev new` refusing\n    to create a plain folder that would shadow a suffixed one already being served\n  - test/auto-root.test.sh, whose 12 assertions run the rendered template on a real Caddy\n\nsite_dir() had to be flipped to match, and that was a live bug rather than a tidy-up: it\nresolved suffixed-first, so on a machine with both folders `ldev standalone` and\n`ldev rehome` would have operated on the folder that ISN'T being served — the exact\nshadowing trap the warnings above exist to name.\n\nWhat master carried that is now gone, per Bryce's decision in the session that produced\ncc7088c: persite as a mode, its template, docs/persite.md, and its two tests. The README\nsections describing it are rewritten rather than deleted — the \"Serving modes\" table\